 "positions_measured": "the eleven periods whose target original is saved (nine companies' newest periods and Marriott 2023/2024), for D04 and D03; B13 at Ford and Enphase, the two companies in the approved scope, whose newest periods are the only saved ones. JPMorgan is refused at period selection (ORDINARY_PERIOD_SELECTION_SAVED_HISTORY_INCOHERENT), the same shard conflict as every other route.",
 "production_authorized": false,
 "question": "B13 (for the two companies the approved definition names), D03 and D04 need model calls. What would they need at the frame's positions, and can any existing response be reused?",
 "record_type": "ISSUE_47_SEMANTIC_ROUTE_REQUEST_NEED",
 "request_identity": {
  "consequence": "semantic_source_id and every request_id differ even where the census is equal, so a response registered for #28's request cannot be matched to a pinned request by identity. The same projection difference was measured before on lodging's source_component_id.",
  "differences": "43 leaves, all in prepared_annual_input and documents[].filing, and the ids that hash them: the ordinary input carries the whole submissions row (11 SEC bookkeeping fields - acceptanceDateTime, act, core_type, fileNumber, filmNumber, isInlineXBRL, isXBRL, isXBRLNumeric, items, primaryDocDescription, size) and the pinned input its five-field projection; the pinned input also carries period_selection and its own selection_rule.",
  "measured_on": "marriott_international 2025-12-31 D04 (identity_diff.py)",
  "units_equal": true
 },
 "requests": {
  "earlier_periods": {
   "D03": 10,
   "D04": 8
  },
  "newest_periods": {
   "B13": 17,
   "D03": 92,
   "D04": 66
  },
  "sum_earlier": 18,
  "sum_newest": 175,
  "sum_total": 193,
  "total": {
   "B13": 17,
   "D03": 102,
   "D04": 74
  }
 },
 "reuse_check": {
  "conclusion": "Nothing here can be replayed: the responses are not in this checkout, would not match a pinned request by identity, and are keyed to another Issue's Requirement. Using them would put #28-authorized calls under #47 positions, which is a cross-Issue credit decision, not an engineering step - and they are results #28 itself has not accepted.",
  "how_they_are_keyed": "input_key hashes (semantic_source_id, requirement_closure_hash): a registration is keyed to #28's requirement closure (issue_28_v14) and to a source id that embeds r6_semantic_source.py's own module hash, so any module change re-keys it by design.",
  "what_they_would_carry": "#28's six D04 results are OPEN runs published WITHHELD with D04_DEFINED_SCOPE_NO_DOUBT_DISCLOSURE, and #28 records real_new_version_semantic_acceptance false and an independent-review blocker (d04_current_development in #28's execution-state.json).",
  "where_registered_responses_live": "capacity_assessment_input.load_registered_input reads ROOT/.git/ordinary-source-authority/{capacity,going-concern}-assessments/<mode>/<key>/ - a private directory inside the checkout that ran the calls. In this checkout that directory holds only two RECORDED_TEST_ONLY capacity entries written by tests; #28's LIVE D04/B13 registrations are on #28's host, as its evidence records (persistent_candidate_root under /Users/.../issue28-2026-09-13)."
 },
 "what_equal_census_means": "For every newest period both routes can reach, the pinned census equals #28's grouped census for the same filing, metric by metric - the model would review the same source units in the same grouping. At the six D04 companies #28 has already run, it also equals #28's actual call count (Marriott 4, Southwest 6, Salesforce 5, Lumen 8, Macy's 5; JPMorgan's 27 is not reachable here). So at the newest year a historical semantic route adds no review #28 is not already doing; the requests that are #47's own are the earlier years, and today only Marriott's two earlier years can be measured.",
